Frontend is now fully wired to the real backend contract, verified by actually running FastAPI (not just reading the source). Here's what changed and what I found.

What's wired to the real API now
Auth — LoginScreen calls POST /api/auth/login for real, shows the server's error message (lockout, bad password), stores the JWT, and a 401 anywhere in the app now bounces back to login automatically.
Nurse Dashboard — Today's Visits, Range Total, Referred Today, and the Weekly Trend chart are computed from live GET /api/visits data. The Top Complaints donut is now a real client-side tally of the complaints field visits return (previously hardcoded numbers).
Visit Records — the table and "Today's Visits" panel both read from GET /api/visits; Sign Out calls the real POST /api/visits/{id}/sign-out and refreshes the list on success.
Fixed a bug I found along the way: AppContext/the modal components existed in the repo but App.jsx never actually mounted them — openModal() calls went nowhere. Added ModalRoot.jsx and wired main.jsx/App.jsx/Sidebar through the real context, so modals now open.
Added vite.config.js proxy so /api/* reaches localhost:8000 in dev without CORS pain.
New files: src/api/{client,auth,visits,lookups}.js, src/hooks/useVisits.js, src/lib/{time,format,insights,notConnected}.js, src/config/navs.js, src/context/{appContextInstance,useApp}.js, src/components/ModalRoot.jsx.

What I deliberately left mocked
AddPatientModal, RequestRestockModal, stock, and admin screens stay local-only — the backend only implements auth and visits (its own README/TODO says so). Patient demographics (type/gender/program/department) also aren't on VisitOut, so those table columns can't be populated yet.

A real bug I found while verifying this
I didn't just read the backend — I actually ran it (FastAPI TestClient + SQLite) to confirm the contract. Login and GET /visits match your frontend exactly. But POST /api/visits and POST /api/visits/{id}/sign-out both crash with A transaction is already begun on this Session — this is a real SQLAlchemy bug, not a SQLite artifact. require_nurse/get_current_user reads the user on the same session FastAPI hands the route (dependency caching), which auto-begins a transaction; visit_service's with db.begin(): then can't begin a second one. This will hit in production too, since it's about MySQL-independent SQLAlchemy session semantics. Fix is on their end (e.g. db.begin_nested() or checking db.in_transaction()), in the sinnz21/Logbook repo, not this project — want me to open an issue/PR there, or just pass this along?

Also confirmed: npm run build and npm run lint both pass clean.
